  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical ball of radius $1 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~m}$ and density $10^5 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$ falls freely under gravity through a distance $h$ before entering a tank of water, If after entering in water the velocity of the ball does not change, then the value of $h$ is approximately:\n(The coefficient of viscosity of water is $9.8 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~N} \\mathrm{~s} / \\mathrm{m}^2$ )"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2296 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2518 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$2249 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2396 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~g}}{9} \\frac{\\mathrm{R}^2\\left[\\rho_{\\mathrm{B}}-\\rho_{\\mathrm{L}}\\right]}{\\eta} \\\\& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\frac{2}{9} \\times \\frac{10 \\times\\left(10^{-4}\\right)^2}{9.8 \\times 10^{-6}}\\left[10^5-10^3\\right] \\\\& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{T}}=224.5\\end{aligned}$\nwhen ball fall from height (h)\n$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{V}=\\sqrt{2 \\mathrm{gh}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{h}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{V}^2}{2 \\mathrm{~g}}\\right)=2518 \\mathrm{~m}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
